WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.497
Warning! Warning!

2
00:00:01.497 --> 00:00:06.705
I built this with AI and text to speech, because I can't narrate for shit!

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:11.597
Hey, Dreamer here, and welcome to the advanced series.

4
00:00:11.597 --> 00:00:17.295
First up: what actually happens when Voyage rolls for you, piece by piece, on the board.

5
00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:24.023
Every rolled action adds up a score, and it starts with the dice: a random part.

6
00:00:24.023 --> 00:00:25.620
Say Nell rolls an eight.

7
00:00:26.067 --> 00:00:27.262
Then her skill.

8
00:00:27.262 --> 00:00:34.832
Knife throwing is level two, times the skill bonus modifier, which is one by default. Plus two.

9
00:00:35.267 --> 00:00:37.758
Then the attribute the skill uses.

10
00:00:37.758 --> 00:00:43.034
Her dexterity is twelve: take away ten, times two and a half. Plus five.

11
00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:45.528
Then a move, if one fits.

12
00:00:45.528 --> 00:00:49.584
Fan Throw's Power is ten, and it goes straight on.

13
00:00:50.033 --> 00:00:55.722
Early in a game there's a head start: plus ten while the game is under fifty ticks old.

14
00:00:56.167 --> 00:00:58.351
Then the difficulty comes off.

15
00:00:58.351 --> 00:01:01.774
I made this one up: a moving target, minus ten.

16
00:01:02.233 --> 00:01:05.507
Add it all up, and Nell's score is twenty five.

17
00:01:05.967 --> 00:01:09.047
The score picks the band on your success levels.

18
00:01:09.047 --> 00:01:15.464
In our world, twenty five to forty nine is Great Success, so the narrator tells it as a great throw.

19
00:01:16.867 --> 00:01:19.667
If the maths lost you, here's the easy version.

20
00:01:19.667 --> 00:01:24.673
Everything good adds up: a bit of luck, how practised you are, how talented you are,

21
00:01:24.673 --> 00:01:28.546
a move if you've got one, and a head start while the game is new.

22
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:31.612
Then how hard the thing is comes off.

23
00:01:32.067 --> 00:01:34.515
Bigger total, better result.

24
00:01:34.515 --> 00:01:36.351
That's all a roll is.

25
00:01:37.767 --> 00:01:40.102
One rule sits on top of all of it.

26
00:01:40.102 --> 00:01:44.085
By default, no single piece can add more than twenty five.

27
00:01:44.085 --> 00:01:49.922
So a move with a Power of thirty still only adds twenty five, and the rest is wasted.

28
00:01:51.333 --> 00:01:56.398
And every part of this board is a setting you can change: how much a skill level counts,

29
00:01:56.398 --> 00:02:00.656
how much an attribute counts, the cap, and where each success band starts.

30
00:02:02.067 --> 00:02:03.111
That's the roll.

31
00:02:03.111 --> 00:02:07.094
Next time, more of the complex stuff I ship in my own worlds.

32
00:02:07.533 --> 00:02:11.481
I'm Dreamer. Now go build something weird, and I'll see you next time!

